{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מזבח קטרת הסמים", :translit "mizbach ktoret ha-samim", :gloss "altar of incense of spices"} {:he "קטרת הסמים", :translit "ktoret ha-samim", :gloss "incense of the spices"} {:he "הסמים", :translit "ha-samim", :gloss "the spices"} {:he "כהן גדול מתעשר בקטור", :translit "kohen gadol mit'aser be-ketor", :gloss "a High Priest is tithed on incense"} {:he "סמים", :translit "samim", :gloss "spices"} {:he "כפרה וסליחה", :translit "kaparah u-slichah", :gloss "atonement and forgiveness"} {:he "שגגת תלמוד עולה זדון", :translit "shegagat talmud olah zaydon", :gloss "an inadvertence of study counts as intentional"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical contrast: the phrase הסמים appears in Lev 4:7 (anointed priest) but is absent in the parallel passage for the congregation (Lev 4:18)."} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on the root ע-ש-ר: the High Priest's incense offering is enriched (מתעשר) with extra spices."}], :frame {:text "The phrase שגגת תלמוד עולה זדון — 'an inadvertence of study counts as intentional' — is rooted in the principle that a scholar's oversight is treated more strictly. Horiyyot 11a teaches that the court's erroneous ruling and the people's resultant inadvertent sin require separate offerings, since the court's error carries its own weight. Gittin 2b–3a discusses how scholars' lapses are judged by a higher standard; Avot 4:16 states שגגת תלמוד עולה זדון. Applying this to the High Priest, whose own error in ritual law is graver, the verse withholds the language of סליחה from his atonement.", :sources ["Horiyyot 11a" "Gittin 2b" "Gittin 3a" "Avot 4:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical contrast: the phrase הסמים appears in Lev 4:7 (anointed priest) but is absent in the parallel passage for the congregation (Lev 4:18).", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay on the root ע-ש-ר: the High Priest's incense offering is enriched (מתעשר) with extra spices.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:06.947281127Z", :model "glm-5.2"}